(2782971, 375112, 60862, '<td valign="top">Interesting idea, to connect a horoscope to the scene before you.  However, at least for me, the composition doesn''t work well.  With a different composition, like putting the paper in the lower left corner while the natural beauty fills the rest of the frame, it would be much better.<br/> <br/>Also, when putting text elements into a picture, I think simpler is better.  I''m not going to spend time reading every one of the visible horoscopes to see anything relevant to the picture.  And if you meant your title to tell me what it says, then again, it needn''t occupy such prominence.<br/> <br/>Unless, of course, your point was to take a picture mostly of the horoscope, in which case I revert back to a picture of horoscopes doesn''t grab me.</td>', 'Interesting idea, to connect a horoscope to the scene before you.  However, at least for me, the composition doesn''t work well.  With a different composition, like putting the paper in the lower left corner while the natural beauty fills the rest of the frame, it would be much better. Also, when putting text elements into a picture, I think simpler is better.  I''m not going to spend time reading every one of the visible horoscopes to see anything relevant to the picture.  And if you meant your title to tell me what it says, then again, it needn''t occupy such prominence. Unless, of course, your point was to take a picture mostly of the horoscope, in which case I revert back to a picture of horoscopes doesn''t grab me.', '2006-09-01 11:20:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(2782972, 388212, 56797, '<td valign="top">wow that looks unreal. so sharp. 9</td>', 'wow that looks unreal. so sharp. 9', '2006-09-01 11:20:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(2782974, 385119, 60862, '<td valign="top">This subject has a lot of potential.  However, your picture suffers from a few problems.  The good news is you can correct all of them either by taking it again or in processing. :)<br/> <br/>First, it''s very low contrast.  Try using the auto levels feature in your software.  Or search Google for "Photoshop levels" or "Photoshop curves."  Many programs other than Photoshop offer those features;  I just find it easiest to find tutorials using Photoshop as a keyword.<br/> <br/>Second, the dead straight-on angle isn''t nearly as interesting as I''m sure you could find.  Try going to one corner, or putting the house in one corner of the pic, or catching the angle of the roof against the sky.<br/> <br/>Finally, and this isn''t as critical as the other two, it''s probably not as sharp as it could be.  It seems like it''s focused fine, but digital photos always are a little blurred in the fine detail when they come out of the camera.  Try playing around with either the sharpen command in your software or experiment with/learn about the "unsharp mask."<br/> <br/>Good luck!</td>', 'This subject has a lot of potential.  However, your picture suffers from a few problems.  The good news is you can correct all of them either by taking it again or in processing. :) First, it''s very low contrast.  Try using the auto levels feature in your software.  Or search Google for "Photoshop levels" or "Photoshop curves."  Many programs other than Photoshop offer those features;  I just find it easiest to find tutorials using Photoshop as a keyword. Second, the dead straight-on angle isn''t nearly as interesting as I''m sure you could find.  Try going to one corner, or putting the house in one corner of the pic, or catching the angle of the roof against the sky. Finally, and this isn''t as critical as the other two, it''s probably not as sharp as it could be.  It seems like it''s focused fine, but digital photos always are a little blurred in the fine detail when they come out of the camera.  Try playing around with either the sharpen command in your software or experiment with/learn about the "unsharp mask." Good luck!', '2006-09-01 11:20:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2782975, 388704, 34938, '<td valign="top">this is superbly creative and I hope it rocks when it comes to score...it tells a story and the composition and colour, wow! it is so interesting that I am looking at it over and over 9</td>', 'this is superbly creative and I hope it rocks when it comes to score...it tells a story and the composition and colour, wow! it is so interesting that I am looking at it over and over 9', '2006-09-01 11:20:57.000000', NULL, 1),
