(2788199, 376291, 35602, '<td valign="top">Nicely composed. REally like the flowers in the foreground.  Need a bit more brightness, though.  It dulled down the detail of the mountains and flowers, though your sky seems perfectly exposed.</td>', 'Nicely composed. REally like the flowers in the foreground.  Need a bit more brightness, though.  It dulled down the detail of the mountains and flowers, though your sky seems perfectly exposed.', '2006-09-02 12:55:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2788200, 375844, 20236, '<td valign="top">I really love everthing about this. 9</td>', 'I really love everthing about this. 9', '2006-09-02 12:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(2788203, 386234, 34192, '<td valign="top">love this.  Think I might have preferred a landscape crop but this works and this is what I see.  There is a whimsicalness about this that I love and I could study it for a while to try and see why they are running, why they are there, why they have violins but then I must think, Why not?  Thank you for this excellent moment, one of my favorites of the challenge. 10 - good luck!</td>', 'love this.  Think I might have preferred a landscape crop but this works and this is what I see.  There is a whimsicalness about this that I love and I could study it for a while to try and see why they are running, why they are there, why they have violins but then I must think, Why not?  Thank you for this excellent moment, one of my favorites of the challenge. 10 - good luck!', '2006-09-02 12:56:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2788205, 388539, 62671, '<td valign="top">That cloud is distracting. very interesting though.</td>', 'That cloud is distracting. very interesting though.', '2006-09-02 12:56:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2788206, 388780, 51538, '<td valign="top">You have captured the dragonlfy-ness of a dragonfly.  Very often, photographers are attracted to these special insects and shoot to capture all.  It is the details - especially the large compound eyes which cover almost 360 degrees - which really tell the insect''s story.  Nice work.</td>', 'You have captured the dragonlfy-ness of a dragonfly.  Very often, photographers are attracted to these special insects and shoot to capture all.  It is the details - especially the large compound eyes which cover almost 360 degrees - which really tell the insect''s story.  Nice work.', '2006-09-02 12:57:03.000000', NULL, 1),
