(2790343, 388127, 19708, '<td valign="top">Good capture and stance here.<br/>The background seems a bit high on the contrast side and would probably benefit from lightening &amp; softening the background.</td>', 'Good capture and stance here.The background seems a bit high on the contrast side and would probably benefit from lightening & softening the background.', '2006-09-02 22:47:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790387, 384133, 19708, '<td valign="top">Love the focal point here and good choice on black &amp; white conversion.<br/>I think this would have had more impact had you used the full 720 pixels instead of 590.</td>', 'Love the focal point here and good choice on black & white conversion.I think this would have had more impact had you used the full 720 pixels instead of 590.', '2006-09-02 23:06:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790391, 385708, 30982, '<td valign="top">Composition works well with the road, the fenceline, and especially the overhanging tree in teh upper right.  Lovely rendition of the colors, too.</td>', 'Composition works well with the road, the fenceline, and especially the overhanging tree in teh upper right.  Lovely rendition of the colors, too.', '2006-09-02 23:07:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790393, 389032, 20941, '<td valign="top">beautiful scene and magnificent sky</td>', 'beautiful scene and magnificent sky', '2006-09-02 23:07:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790394, 388606, 19708, '<td valign="top">A great slice of life represented here and one that could be seen in just about any corner of the world. This image overall, it''s content and tonal levels reminds me of jjbeguin''s work, which is always first-rate.<br/>Well done!</td>', 'A great slice of life represented here and one that could be seen in just about any corner of the world. This image overall, it''s content and tonal levels reminds me of jjbeguin''s work, which is always first-rate.Well done!', '2006-09-02 23:08:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790396, 380178, 20941, '<td valign="top">awesome reflection of those beautiful mountains!</td>', 'awesome reflection of those beautiful mountains!', '2006-09-02 23:08:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790398, 388089, 11738, '<td valign="top">Looks like either the focus is off or its the remains of a heavy cropping job.  Either way, image quality has been compromised.  A very strong composition though.</td>', 'Looks like either the focus is off or its the remains of a heavy cropping job.  Either way, image quality has been compromised.  A very strong composition though.', '2006-09-02 23:09:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790400, 388704, 11738, '<td valign="top">Very cool.</td>', 'Very cool.', '2006-09-02 23:09:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790404, 386643, 20941, '<td valign="top">good eye for a beautiful shot great depth demonstrated by the two figures in the distance. very nice!</td>', 'good eye for a beautiful shot great depth demonstrated by the two figures in the distance. very nice!', '2006-09-02 23:10:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790407, 388083, 19708, '<td valign="top">The curvature of the foreground rocks makes a very nice abstract but is in competition with the water for main focal point. Nice image regardless.</td>', 'The curvature of the foreground rocks makes a very nice abstract but is in competition with the water for main focal point. Nice image regardless.', '2006-09-02 23:11:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790408, 385337, 11738, '<td valign="top">Very interesting image but I fond the light on the squirrel too cold (blue).  Interesting choice of border.</td>', 'Very interesting image but I fond the light on the squirrel too cold (blue).  Interesting choice of border.', '2006-09-02 23:11:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790415, 377423, 30982, '<td valign="top">Great clarity and richness.  A rather intriguing view of this creature!</td>', 'Great clarity and richness.  A rather intriguing view of this creature!', '2006-09-02 23:12:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790417, 388310, 19708, '<td valign="top">Gotta'' love the contrasts and colors here.<br/>The pose and the title are perfect for a composition that can''t help but to bring a warm smile to one''s face.</td>', 'Gotta'' love the contrasts and colors here.The pose and the title are perfect for a composition that can''t help but to bring a warm smile to one''s face.', '2006-09-02 23:12:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790423, 385950, 30982, '<td valign="top">Wonderful rich colors in this.</td>', 'Wonderful rich colors in this.', '2006-09-02 23:14:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790425, 375823, 20941, '<td valign="top">the bold colors add interest to this, the tallest tree looks to be fading a little in the bright sky, but I''m drawn toward your vibrant foreground and mid section</td>', 'the bold colors add interest to this, the tallest tree looks to be fading a little in the bright sky, but I''m drawn toward your vibrant foreground and mid section', '2006-09-02 23:14:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790426, 383555, 19708, '<td valign="top">Pretty tall forrest - just kidding.<br/>Powerful image captured here.<br/>Certainly not a point of view we would get to see very often in life.</td>', 'Pretty tall forrest - just kidding.Powerful image captured here.Certainly not a point of view we would get to see very often in life.', '2006-09-02 23:14:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790431, 388982, 20941, '<td valign="top">vibrant colors, could use more focus on the main subject</td>', 'vibrant colors, could use more focus on the main subject', '2006-09-02 23:15:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790432, 385817, 30982, '<td valign="top">Sweet shot; nice use of DOF.</td>', 'Sweet shot; nice use of DOF.', '2006-09-02 23:15:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790435, 388797, 62671, '<td valign="top">The horizon line could use a straighten.</td>', 'The horizon line could use a straighten.', '2006-09-02 23:17:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790439, 378761, 20941, '<td valign="top">a less distracting background would be more effective to emphasize the  interesting moth you have found. I guess that is his habitat, however, and probably wouldn''t be found in a more photogenic atmosphere</td>', 'a less distracting background would be more effective to emphasize the  interesting moth you have found. I guess that is his habitat, however, and probably wouldn''t be found in a more photogenic atmosphere', '2006-09-02 23:19:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790446, 381288, 20941, '<td valign="top">detailed macro, well composed</td>', 'detailed macro, well composed', '2006-09-02 23:21:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790451, 377518, 33672, '<td valign="top">Gotta love the V-rod! Nice effect and control of the reflection.</td>', 'Gotta love the V-rod! Nice effect and control of the reflection.', '2006-09-02 23:23:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790453, 388782, 33672, '<td valign="top">Great capture! Could be sharper.</td>', 'Great capture! Could be sharper.', '2006-09-02 23:24:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790486, 387738, 43463, '<td valign="top">I really like how you composed this shot. The colors are fabulous too as that they pop off the page. I find it interesting and compelling on the position of the flag - you have the strips facing down and whether it was intentional or not it does make one reflect on the ''fallen'' towers and the fallen. The ones who died and the ones who laid down their lives - the fallen heroes. The fireman in the foreground makes us think of those who gave of themselves on the fateful day of 9/11 - and it doesn''t have to be JUST that day but every day these public servants go out there ''to protect and to save lives''. This photo makes the viewer reflect on their contribution to the Nation. Now, I do have a critique and it is with regards to lighting. I think that you needed to cast more light on the helmet and fireman for he is a bit too much in shadow. Yes, one could say compositionally that plays well into the mood - he is in the shadow because of a pervading sadness with regards to fallen comrades. BUT with less shadows falling on his helmet and left shoulder, the fireman would be much more prominent and have an even greater impact on the photo composition because his uniform will be more visible (especially the crest on the front of the helmet which now rests in shadow and is barely visible).</td>', 'I really like how you composed this shot. The colors are fabulous too as that they pop off the page. I find it interesting and compelling on the position of the flag - you have the strips facing down and whether it was intentional or not it does make one reflect on the ''fallen'' towers and the fallen. The ones who died and the ones who laid down their lives - the fallen heroes. The fireman in the foreground makes us think of those who gave of themselves on the fateful day of 9/11 - and it doesn''t have to be JUST that day but every day these public servants go out there ''to protect and to save lives''. This photo makes the viewer reflect on their contribution to the Nation. Now, I do have a critique and it is with regards to lighting. I think that you needed to cast more light on the helmet and fireman for he is a bit too much in shadow. Yes, one could say compositionally that plays well into the mood - he is in the shadow because of a pervading sadness with regards to fallen comrades. BUT with less shadows falling on his helmet and left shoulder, the fireman would be much more prominent and have an even greater impact on the photo composition because his uniform will be more visible (especially the crest on the front of the helmet which now rests in shadow and is barely visible).', '2006-09-02 23:38:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790518, 387790, 43463, '<td valign="top">The colors are bold and vibrant in these shot. The reds, oranges and golds are very warm hues and as such are more readily equated with the sun rather than the moon. It is the title that tells our eyes not to be deceived. It is the moon that illuminates this field of flowers. Given that, it influences me to think of warm October nights and the illumination of the flowers sets a tone &amp; mood of us glimpsing an otherworldly realm - of magic, fairies, and spirits that walk the earth. The moon is full and it illuminates a magical world rarely seen. My only critique is that there are some drop-out/specks near the moon and some off to the right hand side of the sky. Those can be cloned out so as not to offer distraction.</td>', 'The colors are bold and vibrant in these shot. The reds, oranges and golds are very warm hues and as such are more readily equated with the sun rather than the moon. It is the title that tells our eyes not to be deceived. It is the moon that illuminates this field of flowers. Given that, it influences me to think of warm October nights and the illumination of the flowers sets a tone & mood of us glimpsing an otherworldly realm - of magic, fairies, and spirits that walk the earth. The moon is full and it illuminates a magical world rarely seen. My only critique is that there are some drop-out/specks near the moon and some off to the right hand side of the sky. Those can be cloned out so as not to offer distraction.', '2006-09-02 23:50:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790528, 387498, 30982, '<td valign="top">This is absolutely priceless.  Wonderful capture.</td>', 'This is absolutely priceless.  Wonderful capture.', '2006-09-02 23:52:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790530, 387566, 40797, '<td valign="top">Nice composition! Tyler is so cute!!</td>', 'Nice composition! Tyler is so cute!!', '2006-09-02 23:53:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790533, 387933, 59215, '<td valign="top">Pretty colors, the sun rays make for a nice effect and I like that the trees frame the composition. The horizon line needs to be leveled.</td>', 'Pretty colors, the sun rays make for a nice effect and I like that the trees frame the composition. The horizon line needs to be leveled.', '2006-09-02 23:55:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790534, 388590, 40797, '<td valign="top">BEAUTIFUL!</td>', 'BEAUTIFUL!', '2006-09-02 23:55:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790536, 384660, 40797, '<td valign="top">This is adorable! Great capture!!</td>', 'This is adorable! Great capture!!', '2006-09-02 23:56:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790540, 387130, 43463, '<td valign="top">It is said that ''the eyes are the window to the soul'' and that ''a woman''s eyes are captivating'' but I have never before seen a photo capture a woman''s eyes that are closed AND STILL be captivating &amp; compelling to look at! The composition and color bear a certain individuals style on DPC and indeed you may or may not be said individual;-) Anywho, back the the photo. The colors of violet-blue and green on those eyelashes are stunning and vibrant. She ''fans'' those beautiful colors and the viewer is instantly attracted to her. She is exotic not just in her culteral beauty but in those colors of the eyes. Well done.</td>', 'It is said that ''the eyes are the window to the soul'' and that ''a woman''s eyes are captivating'' but I have never before seen a photo capture a woman''s eyes that are closed AND STILL be captivating & compelling to look at! The composition and color bear a certain individuals style on DPC and indeed you may or may not be said individual;-) Anywho, back the the photo. The colors of violet-blue and green on those eyelashes are stunning and vibrant. She ''fans'' those beautiful colors and the viewer is instantly attracted to her. She is exotic not just in her culteral beauty but in those colors of the eyes. Well done.', '2006-09-02 23:58:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790541, 387872, 63595, '<td valign="top">10, 10, 10 AHHHHHHHHHHHHHH!!!!!!!!!<br/>Wow, that is one amazing picture, how did you get the black so neatly behind the tiger?</td>', '10, 10, 10 AHHHHHHHHHHHHHH!!!!!!!!!Wow, that is one amazing picture, how did you get the black so neatly behind the tiger?', '2006-09-02 23:58:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790544, 388985, 41891, '<td valign="top">just missed the moment!  a fraction of a second later when the running back was about to contact the ball would have had more impact.<br/>clear shot though!</td>', 'just missed the moment!  a fraction of a second later when the running back was about to contact the ball would have had more impact.clear shot though!', '2006-09-02 23:59:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790546, 379749, 40797, '<td valign="top">Wow! Beautiful landscape!!</td>', 'Wow! Beautiful landscape!!', '2006-09-02 23:59:42.000000', NULL, 1),
