(2796332, 388026, 16004, '<td valign="top">this is one of the more effective shots to make use of the enlarged canvas...  there is much to like about this, from the sparkly inviting water, the forest of masts, and the hazy skyline in the background (which complement the masts) all work for me.  the greyscale is very pleasing too.  i''m not entirely sure about the very obvious area of dodging to draw attention to the titular boat.  it feels forced and unnatural.  but overall, the shot has ambience; you can easily place yourself in the frame, hear the sounds of the boats moving...  very nice, and a good choice for the study.  8.</td>', 'this is one of the more effective shots to make use of the enlarged canvas...  there is much to like about this, from the sparkly inviting water, the forest of masts, and the hazy skyline in the background (which complement the masts) all work for me.  the greyscale is very pleasing too.  i''m not entirely sure about the very obvious area of dodging to draw attention to the titular boat.  it feels forced and unnatural.  but overall, the shot has ambience; you can easily place yourself in the frame, hear the sounds of the boats moving...  very nice, and a good choice for the study.  8.', '2006-09-04 13:14:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(2796341, 385287, 35602, '<td valign="top">This was so intriguing, yet so very dark that I had to download it to brighten it.  Once I saw the actual image lighter, I saw the beauty of it.  Any photo that causes me to download it and edit it to see what it is deserves a higher score than what I would ordinarily give it when viewed as is on my monitor.  8</td>', 'This was so intriguing, yet so very dark that I had to download it to brighten it.  Once I saw the actual image lighter, I saw the beauty of it.  Any photo that causes me to download it and edit it to see what it is deserves a higher score than what I would ordinarily give it when viewed as is on my monitor.  8', '2006-09-04 13:17:24.000000', NULL, 1),
