(2810351, 387461, 50641, '<td valign="top">Cool, nice coloration.  Possibly could crop a bit off the top.</td>', 'Cool, nice coloration.  Possibly could crop a bit off the top.', '2006-09-07 13:34:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810353, 387108, 50641, '<td valign="top">Hmm, were there Amish in the Adirondacks?</td>', 'Hmm, were there Amish in the Adirondacks?', '2006-09-07 13:35:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810358, 387933, 30049, '<td valign="top">For a sunset to do well here it needs to be really spectacular.  While this is nice, it''s not out of the ordinary.  Couple other things holding this back are the horizon (not straight) and a centered theme.  I''d bet that 3 minutes prior to this shot the water was reflecting a lot more orange, which could have given this more impact.  All of the above is JMO of course.  ;^)</td>', 'For a sunset to do well here it needs to be really spectacular.  While this is nice, it''s not out of the ordinary.  Couple other things holding this back are the horizon (not straight) and a centered theme.  I''d bet that 3 minutes prior to this shot the water was reflecting a lot more orange, which could have given this more impact.  All of the above is JMO of course.  ;^)', '2006-09-07 13:35:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810361, 385811, 57936, '<td valign="top">This is a bit too soft. If you are going to go in this far you should make it tac-sharp. If you want to go for the soft look, back off a bit and get the flower out to the tips of the petals. It is also hard to determine if the softness is intentional or because of a missed focus point...</td>', 'This is a bit too soft. If you are going to go in this far you should make it tac-sharp. If you want to go for the soft look, back off a bit and get the flower out to the tips of the petals. It is also hard to determine if the softness is intentional or because of a missed focus point...', '2006-09-07 13:36:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810364, 384767, 38732, '<td valign="top">Love the detail of the rocks in the foreground and the wonderful colours from the ones in the background.  The sky is vivid and there seems to be motion from the clouds.  Everything in this shot just comes together so well.  Bumping up!</td>', 'Love the detail of the rocks in the foreground and the wonderful colours from the ones in the background.  The sky is vivid and there seems to be motion from the clouds.  Everything in this shot just comes together so well.  Bumping up!', '2006-09-07 13:36:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810371, 385426, 57936, '<td valign="top">WHOA! Cool boogy board flip! Unfortunately, the colors are a bit flat, the lighting on the subject is too dark, the focus is suspect, and the composition is lacking. It has the WHOA but not the WOW!</td>', 'WHOA! Cool boogy board flip! Unfortunately, the colors are a bit flat, the lighting on the subject is too dark, the focus is suspect, and the composition is lacking. It has the WHOA but not the WOW!', '2006-09-07 13:38:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810378, 386647, 34217, '<td valign="top">very pretty.  I love the saturated colors of the water and sky, but I think you over saturated the rocks.  They just don''t look realy.  However, the photo is so beautiful that i think if would be mean of me to vote down for such a silly thing that is only one one persons opinion.  Good luck 8</td>', 'very pretty.  I love the saturated colors of the water and sky, but I think you over saturated the rocks.  They just don''t look realy.  However, the photo is so beautiful that i think if would be mean of me to vote down for such a silly thing that is only one one persons opinion.  Good luck 8', '2006-09-07 13:40:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810380, 387711, 38732, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous shot with a gorgeous model.  The soft focus really adds a lot to this photo and the bright lighting seems to work the more I look at it.  The model''s wonderful smile and sparkling eyes, captivate me further.  Just beautiful and bumping up!</td>', 'Gorgeous shot with a gorgeous model.  The soft focus really adds a lot to this photo and the bright lighting seems to work the more I look at it.  The model''s wonderful smile and sparkling eyes, captivate me further.  Just beautiful and bumping up!', '2006-09-07 13:40:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810385, 385810, 63163, '<td valign="top">Seems like it maybe a little over-sharpened for my taste, but it does fit the title and makes it seem futuristic. 8</td>', 'Seems like it maybe a little over-sharpened for my taste, but it does fit the title and makes it seem futuristic. 8', '2006-09-07 13:41:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810386, 387741, 30049, '<td valign="top">Yes, this has great color - but there isn''t anything dramatic or artistic about this image.  Feels like a documentary, something you would see in a book showing various bird species.  Nothing wrong with that overall I guess.  The image is sharp and you''ve selected a good aperture to blur out the background while keeping the bird in focus.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', 'Yes, this has great color - but there isn''t anything dramatic or artistic about this image.  Feels like a documentary, something you would see in a book showing various bird species.  Nothing wrong with that overall I guess.  The image is sharp and you''ve selected a good aperture to blur out the background while keeping the bird in focus.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2006-09-07 13:41:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810388, 387216, 57936, '<td valign="top">Nice and sharp around the eyes, but the brows, nose, mouth, and hairline should be a bit sharper. Soft skin is fine, but key points of interest around the face should be sharp. Also, the zipper on the fleece is nice and sharp, leading to the impression that the sharpness around the eyes is post-processing and the softness is not intentional but due to the focal point being off. Also, the skin tone is a bit red, but that I will not knock you for, since it could be the natural skin tone of the young lady. And she is a little cutie!</td>', 'Nice and sharp around the eyes, but the brows, nose, mouth, and hairline should be a bit sharper. Soft skin is fine, but key points of interest around the face should be sharp. Also, the zipper on the fleece is nice and sharp, leading to the impression that the sharpness around the eyes is post-processing and the softness is not intentional but due to the focal point being off. Also, the skin tone is a bit red, but that I will not knock you for, since it could be the natural skin tone of the young lady. And she is a little cutie!', '2006-09-07 13:41:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810396, 387738, 34217, '<td valign="top">Nice photo.  I think your light could have been a lot better.  You are lighting up at him so the shadow from his  nove is almost going up into his eye.  This kind of light can sometimes highlight undesirable facial characteristics like bags under the eye.  You light should almost always be eye level with your subject of above eye leve.  It will give you a nicer lighting pattern.  Plus if you really learn how to use light to your advantage you can minimumize this that people don''t like about themselves.</td>', 'Nice photo.  I think your light could have been a lot better.  You are lighting up at him so the shadow from his  nove is almost going up into his eye.  This kind of light can sometimes highlight undesirable facial characteristics like bags under the eye.  You light should almost always be eye level with your subject of above eye leve.  It will give you a nicer lighting pattern.  Plus if you really learn how to use light to your advantage you can minimumize this that people don''t like about themselves.', '2006-09-07 13:43:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810397, 388068, 57936, '<td valign="top">Well framed by the trees on the outside. Could use to have more detail in the foreground grasses and reeds. Other than the framing, it is compositionally bland and the vanilla sky does nothing to make it more interesting. Technically pretty good, but it does nothing for me...</td>', 'Well framed by the trees on the outside. Could use to have more detail in the foreground grasses and reeds. Other than the framing, it is compositionally bland and the vanilla sky does nothing to make it more interesting. Technically pretty good, but it does nothing for me...', '2006-09-07 13:43:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810399, 384767, 30049, '<td valign="top">Great contrast and detail.  The color may have been pushed a bit too far on saturation IMO.  This would have been a good shot for the subjectless challenge.  ;^)  One last point is that compositionally, the horizon is too much on center I think.  All of the above is JMO of course.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Great contrast and detail.  The color may have been pushed a bit too far on saturation IMO.  This would have been a good shot for the subjectless challenge.  ;^)  One last point is that compositionally, the horizon is too much on center I think.  All of the above is JMO of course.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-09-07 13:44:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810419, 387216, 34217, '<td valign="top">This is way over retouched!!!  Children have beautiful skin and should never require such heavy retouching.  It should be sublte, it need to still look lke you subject (wrinkles and all if you are retouching older folk)  You need to minimize not take every thing out.  The facial expression is really nice and the light is just beautiful, but I am having a hard time getting past that retouching.  Good luck.</td>', 'This is way over retouched!!!  Children have beautiful skin and should never require such heavy retouching.  It should be sublte, it need to still look lke you subject (wrinkles and all if you are retouching older folk)  You need to minimize not take every thing out.  The facial expression is really nice and the light is just beautiful, but I am having a hard time getting past that retouching.  Good luck.', '2006-09-07 13:48:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810422, 388692, 30049, '<td valign="top">I love this shot.  I like the diagonal line created by the branch and the way it leads the viewer to the well placed subject.  Color is good.  It seems like the bird is on the edge of sharpness for the aperture you''ve selected here.  Look at the branch - it''s sharp in front of the birds feet, yet a little fuzzy to the right of the birds head.  Not terrible mind you, just seems like the birds head could be a little sharper.  Of course, it could be my glasses need cleaning or something.  ;^)  Best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', 'I love this shot.  I like the diagonal line created by the branch and the way it leads the viewer to the well placed subject.  Color is good.  It seems like the bird is on the edge of sharpness for the aperture you''ve selected here.  Look at the branch - it''s sharp in front of the birds feet, yet a little fuzzy to the right of the birds head.  Not terrible mind you, just seems like the birds head could be a little sharper.  Of course, it could be my glasses need cleaning or something.  ;^)  Best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2006-09-07 13:48:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810426, 385915, 57936, '<td valign="top">OK Composition, though with the direction the beast is facing, it would do better on the right hand side of the frame. I would have framed it with the animal at the bottom right thirds point. That would also eliminate some of the out-of-focus grass at the front of the image, which is slightly distracting. In particular the change from blur to sharp is too far from the animal. If it were closer, it would not distract. I would either open it up and go for a real shallow DOF on just the animal, with the grass almost ALL creamy with bokeh, or stop it down and get the entire frame sharp and full of small details in the grass. (In case you can''t tell, I cannot determine what kind of deer/antelope/grazing plains animal this is... :) )</td>', 'OK Composition, though with the direction the beast is facing, it would do better on the right hand side of the frame. I would have framed it with the animal at the bottom right thirds point. That would also eliminate some of the out-of-focus grass at the front of the image, which is slightly distracting. In particular the change from blur to sharp is too far from the animal. If it were closer, it would not distract. I would either open it up and go for a real shallow DOF on just the animal, with the grass almost ALL creamy with bokeh, or stop it down and get the entire frame sharp and full of small details in the grass. (In case you can''t tell, I cannot determine what kind of deer/antelope/grazing plains animal this is... :) )', '2006-09-07 13:49:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810433, 384958, 63163, '<td valign="top">The trees seem to dark.  Would like to see more detail in them.</td>', 'The trees seem to dark.  Would like to see more detail in them.', '2006-09-07 13:50:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810438, 388170, 63163, '<td valign="top">Seems a little oversaturated to me.</td>', 'Seems a little oversaturated to me.', '2006-09-07 13:51:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810440, 384958, 57936, '<td valign="top">Nice perspective. Shows the majesty of these venerable titans. However, with so much of the shot being under the forest canopy, I would prefer more detail in the trunks and shadows. With advanced editing, you could always burn the highlights of the sun breaking through at the top.</td>', 'Nice perspective. Shows the majesty of these venerable titans. However, with so much of the shot being under the forest canopy, I would prefer more detail in the trunks and shadows. With advanced editing, you could always burn the highlights of the sun breaking through at the top.', '2006-09-07 13:51:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810441, 388259, 34217, '<td valign="top">Not may people appreciate the art of photographing children. I do, it''s my job.  I think you did a wonderful job.  Her expression is just wonderful, the light is stunning, your framing is wonderful.  Great Job!  If you are not already photographing children for a living, maybe you should be.  Not many photographers like doing or or can do it well. Anyway good luck</td>', 'Not may people appreciate the art of photographing children. I do, it''s my job.  I think you did a wonderful job.  Her expression is just wonderful, the light is stunning, your framing is wonderful.  Great Job!  If you are not already photographing children for a living, maybe you should be.  Not many photographers like doing or or can do it well. Anyway good luck', '2006-09-07 13:51:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810442, 388854, 63163, '<td valign="top">The white tire distracts me.  My eye is drawn the the right corner.</td>', 'The white tire distracts me.  My eye is drawn the the right corner.', '2006-09-07 13:52:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810443, 385192, 34217, '<td valign="top">If you are photographing a person, especially a close up, the eyes really should be in focus instead of the hair.</td>', 'If you are photographing a person, especially a close up, the eyes really should be in focus instead of the hair.', '2006-09-07 13:52:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810446, 388631, 57936, '<td valign="top">Too dark in the areas to which the title is obviously referring. It is entirely unclear what they are or why they are an interesting subject.</td>', 'Too dark in the areas to which the title is obviously referring. It is entirely unclear what they are or why they are an interesting subject.', '2006-09-07 13:52:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810452, 385245, 43463, '<td valign="top">I really like the unusual angle that this is taken from. It really adds visual interest to this picture of a cow. Square crop keeps the main subject the focus of our attention. I look at the title and it innvokes the idea that ol'' bettsy is just a number (0860) from a very large farm of cows that you cannot see in the picture. It calls up the idea of this cow being just one of a large herd all the while it depicts it as an individual in the photograph. The critique I have on this photo is that the lighting on the cows face is too dark that one cannot see it''s eyes. They say the eye''s are the windows to the soul - and when it comes to establishing a connection or human interest to a photo of a person or animal it is the eyes that can really grab &amp; hold the viewer''s attention. Perhaps an slightly slower shutter speed or lower ASA would have let more light come in to illuminate the eyes OR you could use selective editing to up the gamma, brightness &amp; contrast just around the eyes to get them to be more visible.</td>', 'I really like the unusual angle that this is taken from. It really adds visual interest to this picture of a cow. Square crop keeps the main subject the focus of our attention. I look at the title and it innvokes the idea that ol'' bettsy is just a number (0860) from a very large farm of cows that you cannot see in the picture. It calls up the idea of this cow being just one of a large herd all the while it depicts it as an individual in the photograph. The critique I have on this photo is that the lighting on the cows face is too dark that one cannot see it''s eyes. They say the eye''s are the windows to the soul - and when it comes to establishing a connection or human interest to a photo of a person or animal it is the eyes that can really grab & hold the viewer''s attention. Perhaps an slightly slower shutter speed or lower ASA would have let more light come in to illuminate the eyes OR you could use selective editing to up the gamma, brightness & contrast just around the eyes to get them to be more visible.', '2006-09-07 13:53:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810454, 388176, 57936, '<td valign="top">A little flat. I don''t think the B&amp;W is helping here. And the blurred leaf (or whatever you call that part of the bamboo plant) is a distraction.</td>', 'A little flat. I don''t think the B&W is helping here. And the blurred leaf (or whatever you call that part of the bamboo plant) is a distraction.', '2006-09-07 13:54:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810458, 384883, 21915, '<td valign="top">A great capture of Lulworth Cove. Good work</td>', 'A great capture of Lulworth Cove. Good work', '2006-09-07 13:55:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810460, 387130, 63163, '<td valign="top">Vivid eyes.</td>', 'Vivid eyes.', '2006-09-07 13:55:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810461, 388822, 57936, '<td valign="top">Need a longer DOF or better focus overall. Also, it is unclear what the title is referring to. The colors are a bit dull, and the clouds in the distance are uninteresting and blurry.</td>', 'Need a longer DOF or better focus overall. Also, it is unclear what the title is referring to. The colors are a bit dull, and the clouds in the distance are uninteresting and blurry.', '2006-09-07 13:56:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810463, 386384, 21915, '<td valign="top">Good capture of the Red Arrows, perfect timing</td>', 'Good capture of the Red Arrows, perfect timing', '2006-09-07 13:56:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810465, 384105, 63163, '<td valign="top">To dark to me.  Can''t see any detail.</td>', 'To dark to me.  Can''t see any detail.', '2006-09-07 13:57:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810470, 389037, 57936, '<td valign="top">Cute kid. The dark spots on the pillow/blanket in front of her face are a distraction, as is the out-of-focus hair. Compositionally, I would have put her lower in the frame.</td>', 'Cute kid. The dark spots on the pillow/blanket in front of her face are a distraction, as is the out-of-focus hair. Compositionally, I would have put her lower in the frame.', '2006-09-07 13:58:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810473, 379842, 63163, '<td valign="top">Rich colors.</td>', 'Rich colors.', '2006-09-07 13:59:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810476, 388026, 21915, '<td valign="top">Wow this works so well, maybe a little over use of the dodge brush on the back of the yatch, but I like this a lot</td>', 'Wow this works so well, maybe a little over use of the dodge brush on the back of the yatch, but I like this a lot', '2006-09-07 13:59:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810479, 384660, 57936, '<td valign="top">Compositionally uninspirring. The focus could be a bit longer, as the frog is just on the edge of being in focus. I would crop it closer to the frog, since the out-of-focus orange stuff draws the eyes away from the story here.</td>', 'Compositionally uninspirring. The focus could be a bit longer, as the frog is just on the edge of being in focus. I would crop it closer to the frog, since the out-of-focus orange stuff draws the eyes away from the story here.', '2006-09-07 14:00:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810481, 389031, 57936, '<td valign="top">Well composed, good focus, interesting lady! The colors are a bit ruddy, but that is not a major knock.</td>', 'Well composed, good focus, interesting lady! The colors are a bit ruddy, but that is not a major knock.', '2006-09-07 14:01:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810483, 388931, 57936, '<td valign="top">I wish the beak and tail were as sharp as the eye and feet.</td>', 'I wish the beak and tail were as sharp as the eye and feet.', '2006-09-07 14:02:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810490, 388670, 63163, '<td valign="top">Nice touch with the smoke.  I like the border on this one.</td>', 'Nice touch with the smoke.  I like the border on this one.', '2006-09-07 14:03:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810497, 384456, 57936, '<td valign="top">Nice stop action! It would be nice if you could still see the sugar cube (which is, I assume, what made the splash). Also, a slightly longer focus and tighter crop, eliminating the negative space at the top, would improve the image. As it is, the large white space leaves one wondering why the whole cup is not in the frame and the splash is not all in focus?</td>', 'Nice stop action! It would be nice if you could still see the sugar cube (which is, I assume, what made the splash). Also, a slightly longer focus and tighter crop, eliminating the negative space at the top, would improve the image. As it is, the large white space leaves one wondering why the whole cup is not in the frame and the splash is not all in focus?', '2006-09-07 14:05:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810499, 388806, 63163, '<td valign="top">I have these spiders at home.  Not so itsy bitsy!!  Would like this better if the head wasn''t so dark.</td>', 'I have these spiders at home.  Not so itsy bitsy!!  Would like this better if the head wasn''t so dark.', '2006-09-07 14:05:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810502, 388814, 57936, '<td valign="top">A bit too centered. It would be more effective if she were over to the right (her left) about one head width. Also, the bush on the left woudl be better in focus or out of the shot. The background being out of focus is good, but that bush is too close to the subject and distracts. The lighting is also a bit harsh, with too dark of shadows on her face. A slightly different angle or later in the day might have helped, or a reflector or or something to spread a kinder light on your pretty subject.</td>', 'A bit too centered. It would be more effective if she were over to the right (her left) about one head width. Also, the bush on the left woudl be better in focus or out of the shot. The background being out of focus is good, but that bush is too close to the subject and distracts. The lighting is also a bit harsh, with too dark of shadows on her face. A slightly different angle or later in the day might have helped, or a reflector or or something to spread a kinder light on your pretty subject.', '2006-09-07 14:09:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810506, 386459, 23053, '<td valign="top">Nice rhythm...I think I''m spelling that correctly.  Anyway, I like how the colors are glowing, the over-processed look here adds to the effect of the shot.  Good luck.</td>', 'Nice rhythm...I think I''m spelling that correctly.  Anyway, I like how the colors are glowing, the over-processed look here adds to the effect of the shot.  Good luck.', '2006-09-07 14:11:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810509, 381775, 63163, '<td valign="top">Photo seems to dark to me.</td>', 'Photo seems to dark to me.', '2006-09-07 14:12:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810516, 388954, 3214, '<td valign="top">Her stern expression looks anything but dreamy!  Just kidding, well composed and lit.</td>', 'Her stern expression looks anything but dreamy!  Just kidding, well composed and lit.', '2006-09-07 14:14:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810517, 384847, 57936, '<td valign="top">This would be better cropped portrait or with the subject offset more. Also, the visible metal supports in the background are a distraction. You need a less transparent backdrop or dispense with the backdrop and have the background look industrial. As for the model, the stare is reasonably sexy, but the eye make-up is over done and dark patch on the cheek makes her look somewhat sickly or malevolent. Also, the flyaways in the hair look unkempt instead of sexily rumpled, as I expect was the intent. As for the lack of shirt front, it doesn''t hurt the shot, but it isn''t really adding that much to it either. A style of shirt and pose that gave some hint of curves instead of simply showing cleavage would be more enticing.</td>', 'This would be better cropped portrait or with the subject offset more. Also, the visible metal supports in the background are a distraction. You need a less transparent backdrop or dispense with the backdrop and have the background look industrial. As for the model, the stare is reasonably sexy, but the eye make-up is over done and dark patch on the cheek makes her look somewhat sickly or malevolent. Also, the flyaways in the hair look unkempt instead of sexily rumpled, as I expect was the intent. As for the lack of shirt front, it doesn''t hurt the shot, but it isn''t really adding that much to it either. A style of shirt and pose that gave some hint of curves instead of simply showing cleavage would be more enticing.', '2006-09-07 14:14:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810519, 383538, 48717, '<td valign="top">Great picture, composition and exposure, but it seems like there was a bit too much smoothing.  Much of the detail has been lost in the feathers.</td>', 'Great picture, composition and exposure, but it seems like there was a bit too much smoothing.  Much of the detail has been lost in the feathers.', '2006-09-07 14:16:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810522, 388656, 57936, '<td valign="top">If the sky weren''t blown out it would be better. Also, I don''t like the composition. The mountain being further left in the frame, at the expense of the uninteresting left end of the lake, and a crop just below the tree reflections would improve the shot.</td>', 'If the sky weren''t blown out it would be better. Also, I don''t like the composition. The mountain being further left in the frame, at the expense of the uninteresting left end of the lake, and a crop just below the tree reflections would improve the shot.', '2006-09-07 14:17:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810523, 387977, 3214, '<td valign="top">A fine character study!</td>', 'A fine character study!', '2006-09-07 14:17:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810528, 387130, 38732, '<td valign="top">Simply stunning!  I love how the dark hair and angular collar frame the lovely model''s face.  The artistic makeup contrasts wonderfully against the slightly pale skin.  The colour burst from the beautiful lips and eyes are the anchor to this wonderful shot.  A definite fave for me and bumping up!</td>', 'Simply stunning!  I love how the dark hair and angular collar frame the lovely model''s face.  The artistic makeup contrasts wonderfully against the slightly pale skin.  The colour burst from the beautiful lips and eyes are the anchor to this wonderful shot.  A definite fave for me and bumping up!', '2006-09-07 14:18:36.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(2810531, 387056, 3214, '<td valign="top">JMO, but if you cropped this tightly, maybe into a square, bumped the contrast a bit, this would turn into a "wow" shot!</td>', 'JMO, but if you cropped this tightly, maybe into a square, bumped the contrast a bit, this would turn into a "wow" shot!', '2006-09-07 14:19:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810533, 387873, 57936, '<td valign="top">Nice stop action, but it took too long for my eyes to find the splash for the image to work well. The slightly blurry swimmer grabs the eye and it takes a few beats to see the splash, which is the true subject of this image. I think a looser crop would improve that. Also making it more landscape and less square would help.</td>', 'Nice stop action, but it took too long for my eyes to find the splash for the image to work well. The slightly blurry swimmer grabs the eye and it takes a few beats to see the splash, which is the true subject of this image. I think a looser crop would improve that. Also making it more landscape and less square would help.', '2006-09-07 14:20:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810534, 385100, 3214, '<td valign="top">4 degrees of counter clockwise tilt would turn this into a "wow" shot, in my opinion.</td>', '4 degrees of counter clockwise tilt would turn this into a "wow" shot, in my opinion.', '2006-09-07 14:20:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810537, 384456, 48717, '<td valign="top">Good composition and lighting/exposure, but if it were not for the title I would not have a clue as to what is going on here.  Two sugar cubes might have worked better, one to give the splash an one that is about to hit so it gives the stand alone image more meaning.  Make sense?</td>', 'Good composition and lighting/exposure, but if it were not for the title I would not have a clue as to what is going on here.  Two sugar cubes might have worked better, one to give the splash an one that is about to hit so it gives the stand alone image more meaning.  Make sense?', '2006-09-07 14:20:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2810538, 388888, 3214, '<td valign="top">Lovely work, that of a studio pro, methinks!</td>', 'Lovely work, that of a studio pro, methinks!', '2006-09-07 14:21:06.000000', NULL, 1),
