(2815260, 386716, 61679, '<td valign="top">Jeanne,<br/> <br/>A great score considering how tough the competition is in a free study challenge.  I encourage you to revisit this image and play around with different crops.  The center of this flower is exceptional and with the right crop can become a star feature.  One crop I would suggest is to put the center section of the flower at the lower right rule of thirds node while removing the red portion of the background on the left edge of the image.  This makes the flower appear very 3 dimensional and makes it pop out at the viewer.  If you have trouble visualizing my suggestion, send me a PM and I''ll post a thumbnail to my comment.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/></td>', 'Jeanne, A great score considering how tough the competition is in a free study challenge.  I encourage you to revisit this image and play around with different crops.  The center of this flower is exceptional and with the right crop can become a star feature.  One crop I would suggest is to put the center section of the flower at the lower right rule of thirds node while removing the red portion of the background on the left edge of the image.  This makes the flower appear very 3 dimensional and makes it pop out at the viewer.  If you have trouble visualizing my suggestion, send me a PM and I''ll post a thumbnail to my comment. Tim', '2006-09-08 13:34:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(2815264, 386989, 20462, '<td valign="top">good score, but upon further reflection is am absolutely sure i love this image.  it accomplishes what I always try:  to make the viewer enter the image and swim around for a bit.</td>', 'good score, but upon further reflection is am absolutely sure i love this image.  it accomplishes what I always try:  to make the viewer enter the image and swim around for a bit.', '2006-09-08 13:34:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2815282, 386667, 40819, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all who voted this image high, thanks for all the comments both good and not so good.<br/>This is Renee King a very experienced figure model and she is very professional. She was able to move to places before I asked and had a very good awareness of the light and how to use it since she is also a photographer.<br/> <br/>As far as the comments where it was decided the picture was a poor angle or you personally dont like wide angle of the shot and others of the like, well all I can say is to each his own. If you scored me poorly because you have let your personal views cloud your ability to vote, next time move on and dont vote. If you can put aside your personal opinions of the image (unless it is straight and level, dont like wide angle) vote weather you think it is a good image photographically.<br/> <br/>Two things I didnt notice at first when I uploaded it were the light stand leg in the image and the blur of the left arm. Well the blur I knew about but didnt think it would be a problem, if I ever get to shoot a pose like this again Ill use a flash and shoot at a higher shutter speed. The light stand leg? Well I didnt see the forest for the trees, LOL. I was so busy loving Renees back muscles and her tilt that I missed it. Got me on that one.<br/> <br/>Yes she is skinny but no not that skinny she was sitting up straight leaning forward slightly which exaggerated her waistline a bit. I loved the V her back makes and all the shadows showing her frame very clearly. <br/> <br/>You can see more images of Renee on my <a href="//mprnudes.blogspot.com" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Artistic Nude blog here.</a> Enjoy<br/> <br/>Mike<br/></td>', 'Thanks to all who voted this image high, thanks for all the comments both good and not so good.This is Renee King a very experienced figure model and she is very professional. She was able to move to places before I asked and had a very good awareness of the light and how to use it since she is also a photographer. As far as the comments where it was decided the picture was a poor angle or you personally dont like wide angle of the shot and others of the like, well all I can say is to each his own. If you scored me poorly because you have let your personal views cloud your ability to vote, next time move on and dont vote. If you can put aside your personal opinions of the image (unless it is straight and level, dont like wide angle) vote weather you think it is a good image photographically. Two things I didnt notice at first when I uploaded it were the light stand leg in the image and the blur of the left arm. Well the blur I knew about but didnt think it would be a problem, if I ever get to shoot a pose like this again Ill use a flash and shoot at a higher shutter speed. The light stand leg? Well I didnt see the forest for the trees, LOL. I was so busy loving Renees back muscles and her tilt that I missed it. Got me on that one. Yes she is skinny but no not that skinny she was sitting up straight leaning forward slightly which exaggerated her waistline a bit. I loved the V her back makes and all the shadows showing her frame very clearly.  You can see more images of Renee on my Artistic Nude blog here. Enjoy Mike', '2006-09-08 13:45:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2815303, 385245, 4411, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Majanka:</b></div><hr/><i>A lot of comments metioned the fact that the face is to dark</i></td></tr></table> <br/>Just to clarify my comment. I can see the eyes, but only just. I just felt that they needed bringing out a bit more. I have a reasonably well calibrated CRT btw.<br/>I think it''s the backlighting causing the eyes to be in shadow rather than the overall brightness which is the issue on my monitor so don''t worry about it too much.<br/> <br/>Still a brilliant shot : )</td>', 'Originally posted by Majanka:A lot of comments metioned the fact that the face is to dark Just to clarify my comment. I can see the eyes, but only just. I just felt that they needed bringing out a bit more. I have a reasonably well calibrated CRT btw.I think it''s the backlighting causing the eyes to be in shadow rather than the overall brightness which is the issue on my monitor so don''t worry about it too much. Still a brilliant shot : )', '2006-09-08 13:57:44.000000', NULL, 0),
