(2816445, 377518, 53763, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BradP:</b></div><hr/><i> Certainly a unique image here in this challenge.<br/>The post-processing has taken this out of the realm of photography in my opinion. Have you tried this in a high-contrast black &amp; white? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>i respectfully disagree. every photograph essentially is an approximation. what your eyes see and what your sensor captures can almost never be the same.<br/> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.hosca.com/images/IMG_20060805_3018_bw.jpg'', strrpos(''//www.hosca.com/images/IMG_20060805_3018_bw.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.hosca.com/images/IMG_20060805_3018_bw.jpg"/></td>', 'Originally posted by BradP: Certainly a unique image here in this challenge.The post-processing has taken this out of the realm of photography in my opinion. Have you tried this in a high-contrast black & white?   i respectfully disagree. every photograph essentially is an approximation. what your eyes see and what your sensor captures can almost never be the same. ', '2006-09-08 22:07:41.000000', NULL, 0),
