(2819133, 387498, 40106, '<td valign="top">PERFECT!!! Didn''t get to vote on this one but i definitely would''ve given it a 10!!!  So cute and I love the feeling of anticipation you captured!</td>', 'PERFECT!!! Didn''t get to vote on this one but i definitely would''ve given it a 10!!!  So cute and I love the feeling of anticipation you captured!', '2006-09-10 01:13:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2819164, 380852, 32997, '<td valign="top">maybe you should try using two hands next time...:-)<br/>I love how the greatest intensity of the clouds seems to be waiting for you at the end of the road..</td>', 'maybe you should try using two hands next time...:-)I love how the greatest intensity of the clouds seems to be waiting for you at the end of the road..', '2006-09-10 01:23:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2819165, 387181, 40106, '<td valign="top">so so so so sooooo cool!! the colors are soooo tasteful... my eyes don''t want to look away!!!  goshhhh that blue is soooo nice!</td>', 'so so so so sooooo cool!! the colors are soooo tasteful... my eyes don''t want to look away!!!  goshhhh that blue is soooo nice!', '2006-09-10 01:23:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2819191, 387806, 53147, '<td valign="top">Man - I wish I had been able to vote on this challenge. So much good stuff. This one struck me as I breezed through the entries. A diferent type of shot for a Free STudy and very well done. The processing really takes this way beyond a pic of ordinary daily stuff and well into art - and very good art at that. Great lines, perfect crop and composition and the b&amp;w contrasty feel is wonderful. The 15 voters who gave you below 4 must have been wanting pretty people, perfect landscapes or close up animals and not willing to give it up for something artistically different. Very nice eye on taking the pic and excellent postprocessing Deb. You would have scored very well with me.</td>', 'Man - I wish I had been able to vote on this challenge. So much good stuff. This one struck me as I breezed through the entries. A diferent type of shot for a Free STudy and very well done. The processing really takes this way beyond a pic of ordinary daily stuff and well into art - and very good art at that. Great lines, perfect crop and composition and the b&w contrasty feel is wonderful. The 15 voters who gave you below 4 must have been wanting pretty people, perfect landscapes or close up animals and not willing to give it up for something artistically different. Very nice eye on taking the pic and excellent postprocessing Deb. You would have scored very well with me.', '2006-09-10 01:34:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2819355, 387790, 36999, '<td valign="top">Wow, Jon, this is really cool!  Where is that field??  Excellent treatment.</td>', 'Wow, Jon, this is really cool!  Where is that field??  Excellent treatment.', '2006-09-10 02:25:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2819426, 387540, 31403, '<td valign="top">didn''t see this in the challenge - but just love it.<br/> <br/>How do you get that softness in there?  is that a Glam Glow action?  It sure is cool.<br/> <br/>This is art that is worthy to hang on many walls!  Really has a timeless, every person''s memory kind of feel to it.  I related to it instantly - ah the magic of photography.<br/> <br/>This is very nice work - you should be proud to have a shot like this in your portfolio.</td>', 'didn''t see this in the challenge - but just love it. How do you get that softness in there?  is that a Glam Glow action?  It sure is cool. This is art that is worthy to hang on many walls!  Really has a timeless, every person''s memory kind of feel to it.  I related to it instantly - ah the magic of photography. This is very nice work - you should be proud to have a shot like this in your portfolio.', '2006-09-10 02:52:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2819514, 381899, 62093, '<td valign="top">Congratulations to my son, Jeffrey, on a beautiful photo!  You deserve all the praise you get.<br/>Mom</td>', 'Congratulations to my son, Jeffrey, on a beautiful photo!  You deserve all the praise you get.Mom', '2006-09-10 03:56:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2819518, 388217, 31533, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pineapple:</b></div><hr/><i> It''s a nice tehcnique.  My question, why f11? when you had the camera on a tripod and might have had a larger depth of field with f22.  Excuse my ignorance... ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It was my intention to use a shallow depth of field.<br/>I have the same shot taken at f/22 and even at f/30 but those just don''t work as well as this one.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by pineapple: It''s a nice tehcnique.  My question, why f11? when you had the camera on a tripod and might have had a larger depth of field with f22.  Excuse my ignorance... ;-)   It was my intention to use a shallow depth of field.I have the same shot taken at f/22 and even at f/30 but those just don''t work as well as this one.', '2006-09-10 04:02:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2819525, 387086, 57701, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jaded_youth:</b></div><hr/><i> kinda odd. not sure where to go with this.that middle reflection looks really cool almost like japenese writing but the other two just look like blobs so i guess that wasnt your intention. or that second one was a cool mistake. looks like rocks in a frying pan. that doesnt say much to me. 5 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You are right!! I put the stones in a frying pan with water and a lamp behind. I moved the container for having the strange glares. Sorry for my english I hope you can understand :D</td>', 'Originally posted by jaded_youth: kinda odd. not sure where to go with this.that middle reflection looks really cool almost like japenese writing but the other two just look like blobs so i guess that wasnt your intention. or that second one was a cool mistake. looks like rocks in a frying pan. that doesnt say much to me. 5   You are right!! I put the stones in a frying pan with water and a lamp behind. I moved the container for having the strange glares. Sorry for my english I hope you can understand :D', '2006-09-10 04:07:53.000000', NULL, 0),
